ystem is a critical infrastructure component responsible for managing train movements and ensuring safety across the M1 Metro Line. It is centrally managed by Central Traffic Control, which oversees and coordinates train operations to maintain safe and efficient service. Specifically, the Signaling System controls train movements at both Station 35 and Station 36, as well as between all stations along the M1 Metro Line. By integrating control across individual stations and the entire line, the system ensures that train operations are conducted smoothly, minimizing risks and optimizing traffic flow throughout the network.", "INCIDENT: STATION 36 UNAVAILABILITY:A potential incident where Station 36 becomes unavailable, requiring passengers to use Station 35 or Station 37 as alternatives, and possibly resulting in trains passing through without stopping. Emergency evacuation routes are activated.", "INCIDENT: VENTILATION SYSTEM A FAILURE:A potential incident where Ventilation System A fails, affecting both Station 36 and Station 35 due to the shared system.", "NACHALAT YEHUDA:Nachalat Yehuda is the neighborhood served by Station 36, indicating the station's catchment area.", "CENTRAL TRAFFIC CONTROL:Central Traffic Control is the system responsible for managing and controlling the Signaling System at both Station 35 and Station 36. It oversees train movements and ensures safety by coordinating the signaling infrastructure at these stations. Through its centralized management, Central Traffic Control plays a critical role in maintaining efficient and secure train operations across multiple locations.", "TRANSFORMER 36A:Transformer 36A is the specific transformer connecting Station 36 to the Central Power Grid.", "JABOTINSKY STREET:", "TRANSFORMER 35A:Transformer 35A is the specific transformer connecting Station 35 to the Central Power Grid.", "CRITICAL INFRASTRUCTURE FAILURE:A potential incident where Ventilation System A fails, resulting in the loss of ventilation for both Station 35 and Station 36, possibly requiring evacuation and affecting approximately 80,000 daily passengers.", "BUSINESS DISTRICT ENTRANCE:The Business District Entrance is one of the two entrances to Station 35, providing access from the Kiryat Arie business district.", "RESIDENTIAL ENTRANCE:The Residential Entrance is one of the two entrances to Station 35, providing access from the residential area.", "M1 SEGMENT:The M1 segment is the initial segment of the metro line on which Station 35 is the northernmost station.", "CUT-AND-COVER:Cut-and-cover is the construction method used for building Station 35 and Station 36.", "2019-2024 CONSTRUCTION PERIOD:The 2019-2024 construction period refers to the timeframe during which Station 35 and Station 36 were built by Shapir Engineering.", "M1 METRO LINE:The M1 Metro Line is Israel's first underground metro system, serving the Tel Aviv metropolitan area, running from Petah Tikva to Tel Aviv's central business district, with planned extensions to Bat Yam. It includes multiple stations and is a major public transportation project."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-large"}}, "key": "embeddings_9ecae80320a01a15c073c3a87d1e282c0d1fa29e55515f62d088d92386b84417_v2"}